                <pb facs="1034" n="914" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg914"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister O’Brien to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. O’Brien reports that he has been informed by the secretary of state for
                    foreign affairs that the <hi rendition="#italic">Agnes G. Donahoe</hi> case will
                    be decided, leniently, by July 22.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
